# The Black Row (side quest, docs/story/side_quests.md): once the Martikovs are home, the Seventh Row comes up black
# every night and is bare by morning. Somebody picks it in the dark: Adrian, who eats the black grapes because they
# make him dream of Elvir alive and not angry. The row is a cutting of the Gulthias tree that Kostin planted under it
# on Ruxandra's last order, and it has its own roots now, whatever happened on Yester Hill. Cutting into it wakes the
# Vine Mother (data/monsters/vine_mother.json). Reached from Andrei the picker (hands:picker), Davian's "Heard anything
# interesting?" (davian:menu) and the row itself (prop seventh_row). Once the Black Row is under way and the Gulthias
# tree has burned, his news is the lantern on Yester Hill (The Druid Who Came Back). Every line here is unvoiced for now.

# --- Davian's news (davian:menu jumps here) ---

~ davian_news
if quest.the_black_row and flag.gulthias_tree_burned and level >= 7 and quest.the_druid_who_came_back != done
-> yester_hill/the_druid_who_came_back:davian_news
endif
if quest.the_black_row == done
Davian: The Seventh Row's in again. Young vines. Adrian waters them himself and won't let anyone else hold the can. It's a family failing.
elif quest.the_black_row and quest.the_black_row != rumored
Davian: The Seventh Row. You know as much as I do. Go and sit in it after dark.
else
quest the_black_row asked
Davian: Interesting. Hm. The Seventh Row. My grandfather planted it, and Elvir pruned it from the day he could hold the knife. It's coming up black. Black grapes every night, and every morning, bare.
Davian: Somebody picks it in the dark. My pickers won't go near it. Find out who. If it's druids, I want them. If it isn't, I want to know what it is before I burn my grandfather's vines.
endif
-> wizard_of_wines/davian:menu

# --- The Seventh Row (prop seventh_row) ---

~ row
if quest.the_black_row == done
Narrator: The Seventh Row is young vines on new stakes, and a long scar of turned earth where something was dug out by the roots. Somebody has planted rosemary at the end of it.
-> END
endif
if flag.vine_mother_slain
Narrator: A long trench of torn earth and black splinters where the Seventh Row was. It smells of spilt wine.
-> END
endif
Narrator: The last row before the camp. The leaves are veined dark, like the back of an old hand, and the grapes hang in heavy black clusters, far too many and far too ripe for this valley.
* [if night and quest.the_black_row] (Wait in the vines and see who comes.) -> stakeout
* [if not flag.black_row_nature] [Nature DC 13] (Look at where the vine meets the root.) -> nature | nature_missed
* [if not flag.black_row_feathers] [Investigation DC 13] (Look at the ground between the rows.) -> feathers | feathers_missed
* (Leave it.) -> END

~ nature
set black_row_nature
Narrator: These aren't the Martikovs' vines any more. Something has grown up into every rootstock in the row and is wearing the vines like sleeves. The wood under the bark is black and wet, and it's warm.
interject class:cleric: That's no vine. That's a blight, and a big one, and it's all one plant.
-> row

~ nature_missed
Narrator: Black grapes. Too many. That's all you can tell.
-> row

~ feathers
set black_row_feathers
Narrator: Black feathers in the furrow, a lot of them, and footprints: bare feet, a man's, that start in the middle of the row from nothing, as if he'd dropped out of the sky, and walk to the end and back.
interject tag:curious: Someone comes here as a bird and leaves as a man.
-> row

~ feathers_missed
Narrator: Trodden earth and fallen leaves. Pickers, probably.
-> row

# --- The night watch ---

~ stakeout
time until 1
Narrator: An hour past midnight a raven comes down into the Seventh Row, and shakes itself, and is Adrian Martikov in his shirtsleeves, with his hat in his hand.
Narrator: He picks the black grapes by feel, without looking, a whole hat full. He eats them standing there, one after another, with his eyes shut.
if flag.elvir_buried
Narrator: Then he walks to the end of the row, where his brother is buried, and sits down with his back to the cairn, and talks, very quietly, as if somebody were answering.
else
Narrator: Then he lies down in the furrow between the vines, and talks, very quietly, as if somebody were answering.
endif
* (Step out of the vines.) -> confront

~ confront
quest the_black_row the_picker
Adrian [afraid]: You. Of course you. Don't tell Father. Or tell him. He'll only say he knew.
Adrian: When I eat them I dream of Elvir. He's alive, and he's on the hill, and he isn't angry with me. That's all. That's all it is. One hat a night.
Narrator: He holds up his hands to show you he's harmless, and in the moonlight you can see the veins on the backs of them. They are dark, and they branch, like the leaves.
* [if flag.martikovs_reconciled] Your father forgave you. Elvir would have too, without the grapes. -> convinced
* [if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled] Elvir ordered you to fly. He'd order you to stop. -> convinced
* [Persuasion DC 15] That isn't Elvir. It's the tree from the hill, wearing his face, and it's drinking you. -> convinced | not_convinced
* (Draw steel and cut into the root.) -> cut

~ convinced
set adrian_against_row
Narrator: Adrian looks at his hands for a long time. Then he puts his hat back on, which is the most decided thing you have ever seen him do.
Adrian: Then help me pull it up. All of it. Whatever it is.
join adrian_martikov
-> wakes

~ not_convinced
Adrian: No. Not yet. One more night. You'd want one more night.
Narrator: He's a raven before you can answer, going away over the vines toward the house.
-> cut

~ cut
Narrator: Your blade goes into the black wood at the foot of the row, and the whole row flinches, from one end to the other.
-> wakes

~ wakes
cutscene sq_vine_mother
Narrator: The earth heaves. The Seventh Row stands up out of the ground: every vine of it one plant, one great dark mass of root and vine-wood, rising twice the height of the house, dripping black wine from every branch.
if flag.elvir_buried
Narrator: In the bark at the heart of it there's a face, almost a young man's, almost a Martikov's. It isn't. It has only been drinking from one.
endif
if flag.gulthias_tree_burned
interject tag:blunt: The tree on the hill burned. We watched it.
Narrator: It did. This one had its own roots by then, and something to drink.
endif
combat vine_mother

# --- After (davian:menu jumps here) ---

~ report
set black_row_paid
quest the_black_row done
if flag.adrian_against_row
Narrator: Adrian walks in beside you, black sap to the elbows, and stands in front of his father, and tells him all of it before you can.
Davian: Hm.
Narrator: Davian takes his son's hands and turns them over in his own. The dark veins are fading already, back to plain blue.
Davian [sad]: A hat a night, for a dream. You could have told me. I'd have sat in the row with you. I dream of him too, boy. I don't need grapes.
else
Narrator: Adrian is waiting by his father's chair when you come in, black sap on his cuffs, and doesn't look up.
Davian: He told me. Some of it. Enough. We'll talk about the rest when we've both drunk enough to manage it.
endif
Davian: My grandfather's row, and you cut it out by the roots. Good. It wasn't his any more.
Davian: The wizard who gave us the stones left this in the press-house rack a hundred years ago, against the day something in the vines needed burning. I always thought it was a joke. It turns out he was a better farmer than he looked.
if guest:adrian_martikov
leave adrian_martikov
endif
give wand_of_fireballs
gold +250
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +1 ratatoille +2 wren_featherfoot +1: You cut the Black Row out of the Martikovs' vineyard
-> wizard_of_wines/davian:menu
